  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Iron (Fe) is used to obtain Curmetal from CuSO, (aq) because Fe is more reactive than Cu (and also easly available and is cheaper) thus, replace the copper from CuSO $_{4}$ to give copper (Cu)\r\n$\\mathrm{CuSO}_{4}(\\mathrm{aq})+\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{s}) \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{FeSO}_{4}(\\mathrm{aq})+\\mathrm{Cu}(\\mathrm{s})$",
